  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nSurface high pressure will drift slowly east tonight into Monday, \nbut the ridge axis will still be extending westward back across our \narea. This will result in another night of good radiational cooling \nacross our area. Will generally have lows in the mid to upper 30s, \nbut some lower 30s will be possible in outlying/sheltered areas. \nHave issued a Frost Advisory for our entire area for tonight. \n\nHigh pressure will remain in control of the weather through the rest\nof the week. This will result in dry and seasonable temperatures \nthrough the forecast period.",
